\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A flat plane and the remaining inner masses}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Let the last plane of \ref{fdip-01CB} have flux zero and suppose every plane, including this one, satisfies its scalar angle bound. The plane can first be deformed with the others to constant curvature by \ref{fdip-01A4}. Its two shifts then commute even when either has a nontrivial cycle holonomy. In the count of \ref{fdip-01CA} the two ends of each translated pair have precisely the same eigenangle. Thus every angular fiber has a partner on its own arc and the endpoint signature is zero, whatever the three inner half-signatures are.}
